    "title": "Frog Jump with K Distance",
    "category": "Dynamic Programming",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "A frog stands on the first stone and may jump forward up to K stones at a time. The energy cost of a jump is the absolute difference between the heights of the starting and destination stones. Determine the minimum total energy required to reach the last stone.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains integers N and K. \u2022 Second line contains N integers.",
    "output": "Print the minimum energy required.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 2 \u2264 N \u2264 10^5 \u2022 1 \u2264 K \u2264 100"
